pr_body:
This PR fixes #11387, #11224

ExternalDependency objects are created in the ReplacementScan, which runs as part of the bind phase.
When the DuckDBPyRelation is created, it first creates a Relation, this gets bound to verify the correctness and also to collect the names+types that are returned from the query.

The ExternalDependency objects were not being forwarded anywhere and they died together with the rest of the bind data that was not used.

As a result, the objects that the query has discovered during Bind were not being kept alive by us, and would thus get deleted if no longer referenced (as evidenced by the referenced issue, where the DataFrame has gone out of scope)

## Internal details

ExternalDependency is now a collection of DependencyItems, which is a pure virtual class that can hold anything.
We implement the PythonDependencyItem to hold the RegisteredObject.

When the QueryRelation is created we add an ExternalDependency into the TableRef, when we bind it, we create a Copy() which also gets the ExternalDependency.
During the ReplacementScan this gets populated with the objects we depend on (and also the ones we have created)

This now means that the objects are guaranteed to stay alive as long as the DuckDBPyRelation is alive, and because it's the TableRef that is responsible for this, this extends to VIEWs created from the Relation.

### ReplacementScanInput

```c++
struct ReplacementScanInput {
public:
	ReplacementScanInput(TableRef &ref, const string &table_name) : ref(ref), table_name(table_name) {
	}

public:
	TableRef &ref;
	const string &table_name;
};
```

The `TableRef` is provided to the ReplacementScan function, in the Python client we use this as a cache for the replacement scan. When the object exists in the cache (ExternalDependency) it gets used, otherwise we perform the scan, for a successful scan we populate the cache.

### TableFunctionBindInput

The `TableFunctionRef` is provided to the TableFunction's bind function, this gives it the chance to take a reference on the DependencyItem(s) created during replacement scan, making sure it stays alive during execution.

This is used for the `arrow_scan`, in the replacement scan we create a `PythonTableArrowArrayStreamFactory` that needs to stay alive during execution.
